sd: under LOK a key that starts text edit finishes before the next

A printable key on a selected text object, or Enter on one, starts text
edit through an asynchronous SID_ATTR_CHAR. LOK posts each key as its
own event, so keys already queued behind the first run before the edit
begins: Ctrl+Home after "a" moved nothing and the next letters landed at
the end (Ely: macOS under load, 1 run in 10). Under LOK the dispatch is
synchronous. ViewShell::KeyInput holds the current function while it
handles the key, since the dispatch replaces that function.
--- a/sd/source/ui/func/fupoor.cxx
+++ b/sd/source/ui/func/fupoor.cxx
